.TH LINUXCNCTOP "1"  "2026-07-31" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
linuxcnctop \- live LinuxCNC status display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxcnctop
[\fI\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fI\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR] [\fI\-\-width\fR \fIW\fR] [\fI\-\-height\fR \fIH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlinuxcnctop\fR displays the LinuxCNC state in a live format similar to the
Linux "top" command: one row per status field, with recently changed values
highlighted.

It is a web application served by the running controller, opened in a window by
\fBgmcui\fR(1). The server is taken from the \fBGMC_REST_URL\fR environment
variable (default http://127.0.0.1:5080) and the task instance from
\fBGMC_INSTANCE\fR (default \fImilltask\fR); the same page can be opened in any
browser at \fI/app/linuxcnctop/\fR.

Lengths are displayed in millimetres, the unit the controller keeps internally,
regardless of the machine's configured units.

For a headless machine or for pasting into a bug report, use
\fBlinuxcnctop\-dump\fR(1), which prints the same status as text.

It is more fully documented in the AXIS GUI documentation but can be run
standalone or with other GUIs.
http://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/gui/axis.html

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBlinuxcnctop\-dump(1)\fR, \fBgmcui(1)\fR, \fBLinuxCNC(1)\fR

Much more information about LinuxCNC and HAL is available in the LinuxCNC
and HAL User Manuals, found at /usr/share/doc/LinuxCNC/.

.SH BUGS
None known at this time. 
